{"name":"Black Heron","hex":"#444647","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"},{"term":"heron","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any long-legged, long-necked wading bird of the family Ardeidae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heron"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black heron","blocks":[{"text":"The black heron, also known as the black egret, is an African heron. It uses its wings to form a canopy when fishing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Black_heron%2C_Egretta_ardesiaca%2C_at_Marievale_Nature_Reserve%2C_Gauteng%2C_South_Africa._%2825201552667%29.jpg/330px-Black_heron%2C_Egretta_ardesiaca%2C_at_Marievale_Nature_Reserve%2C_Gauteng%2C_South_Africa._%2825201552667%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_heron","wikidata":"Q392175"},{"title":"Heron","blocks":[{"text":"Herons are long-legged, long-necked, freshwater and coastal birds in the family Ardeidae, with 75 recognised species, some of which are referred to as egrets or bitterns rather than herons. Members of the genus Botaurus are referred to as bitterns, and, together with the zigzag heron, or zigzag bittern, in the monotypic genus Zebrilus, form a monophyletic group, Botaurinae, within the Ardeidae family. Egrets do not form a biologically distinct group from herons, and tend to be named differently because they are mainly white or have decorative plumes in breeding plumage. Herons, by evolutionary adaptation, have long beaks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Ardeidae-01.jpg/330px-Ardeidae-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heron","wikidata":"Q18789"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black","wikidata":"Q23445"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Black_Heron.jpg/500px-Black_Heron.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Black_Heron.jpg/1280px-Black_Heron.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Black_Heron.jpg/500px-Black_Heron.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lake Naivasha - Kenya","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlack_Heron.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Balck_Heron_canopy_crop.jpg/500px-Balck_Heron_canopy_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Balck_Heron_canopy_crop.jpg/500px-Balck_Heron_canopy_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org